Z||000000||Formula88||06-24-2001||04:12 PM||||Just wanted to let everyone know I got my 180* thermostat and low temp fan switch from Rodney and put it on this weekend.  Love it!  The fan comes on before the needle is past the half-way mark.  Runs nice and cool.  Perfect OEM look to the switch, too.  But, boy was that switch a PITA to get the wiring off with my fat fingers!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000001||FieroJoe||06-24-2001||10:53 PM||||I have the 180 thermostat, and the needle never gets past the first mark on the gauge (about 1/4 of the way), and it will just cover the line if it is a hot day and I've been doing a whole lot of driving.<P>Don't know why that is though...I'm pretty sure that the gauge is calibrated properly!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||06-24-2001||11:58 PM||||Well, my fan kicks on just past the second small mark past the large quarter mark (if that makes any sense).  Still never gets up half way (220*).  I like it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||7
